diff --git a/Source/ThirdParty/sml/README-apotheosis.md b/Source/ThirdParty/sml/README-apotheosis.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..43a1d07ac2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Source/ThirdParty/sml/README-apotheosis.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Boost.SML (vendored for Project Apotheosis)
+
+`sml.hpp` is the single-header [Boost].SML state machine library, vendored
+verbatim for the TileGrid v2 rewrite (see `docs/TILEGRID-DESIGN.md` §2.2b).
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| upstream | https://github.com/boost-ext/sml |
+| version | **v1.2.0** (tag `v1.2.0`, `BOOST_SML_VERSION 1'2'0`) |
+| source | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/boost-ext/sml/v1.2.0/include/boost/sml.hpp |
+| license | Boost Software License 1.0 (`LICENSE_1_0.txt`, upstream `LICENSE.md`) |
+| requires | C++14 (Clang 3.4+, GCC 5.1+, MSVC 2015+) |
+
+Nothing was modified. Update by re-downloading the file for a new tag and
+updating this table.
+
+## Why it is here
+
+The tile grid model (`Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/texmap/
+TextureMapperTileGridMachines.h`) writes its five lifecycles - tile, dirty
+patch, grid, replay job, store phase - as SML transition tables: no
+allocation, no RTTI, no exceptions, compile-time dispatch, and an unhandled
+event is reported instead of silently ignored, which is invariant I16 of the
+plan.
+
+## Where it may be included from
+
+Only from `TextureMapperTileGridMachines.h` and the two `.cpp` files that
+include it, plus the host tests in `Project-Apotheosis/tests/tilegrid/`.
+It must not leak into `TextureMapperTileGridModel.h` or any other WebCore
+header, so the rest of the engine never sees it.
